  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "The Commissioner vs K. Velan on 25 November, 2024 Author: R. Suresh Kumar Bench: R. Suresh Kumar, C. Saravanan W.A.No. In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 25.11.2024 Coram : The Honourable Mr.Justice R. Suresh Kumar And The Honourable Mr.Justice C. Saravanan W.A.No.1311 of 2024 1. The Commissioner Food Safety and Drug Administration Guindy, Chennai 32. 2. The Government Analyst Food Analysis Laboratory Guindy, Chennai 32. .. Appel Vs. K. Velan .. Respo Prayer: Appeal filed under Clause 15 of the Letters Patent Act, against the order dated 30.10.2023 in W.P.No.16005 of 2022. For the Appellants : Mr.Kumaresan Additional Advocate Gen assisted by Mr.K.Tippu Government Advocate For the Respondent : Mr.S.Sivakumar JUDGMENT The Commissioner vs K. Velan on 25 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/57297622/ 1 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 2.1.",
    "facts": "The respondent, who was the writ petitioner, was placed under suspension on 26.09.2019 for the reason that he indulged in a criminal case for the alleged offence punishable under Section 302 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860. Apart from the criminal case that was pending against him, Departmental Proceedings since has also been initiated, he was placed under suspension with effect from 26.09.2019 and he had been given subsistence allowance of 50% of his pay with effect from 24.09.2019 till 23.03.2020. 2.3. Pursuant to the said directions issued by this Court, the employer, having considered the plea of the writ petitioner, passed orders on 03.06.2022, whereby, reiterated that proceedings under Rule 17(b) of the Tamil Nadu Government Servants (Discipline and https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Appeals) Rules, 1955, is pending apart from the criminal case and in such circumstances, under F.R.53(1)(A)(iii) and as per the Government Letter dated 02.09.1976 , if the suspension is prolonged beyond six months' period, for which the direct reason is attributable to the Government servant, then, the subsistence allowance can be reduced from 50% to 25%. 2.4. . Hence, the learned Single Judge was pleased to allow the said writ petition by setting aside the order dated 03.06.2022 and directed the employer to enhance the subsistence allowance to 75% from the date he has completed six months' period of the suspension.",
    "arguments": "Therefore, on that ground also the writ petitioner is not entitled to get the benefit of subsistence allowance https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis of 75% as has been sought. Therefore, there has been every justification on the part of the employer to reject the said plea through the impugned order before the Writ Court dated 03.06.2022. When that being so, absolutely there has been no reason on the part of the employer to reduce the subsistence allowance from 50% to 25%. However, the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis said Rule would not be invoked in the present circumstances of the case, since the issue has been considered threadbare by the learned Single Judge in the order impugned. Therefore, the counsel appearing for the respondent would submit that the order impugned does not warrant any interference at the hands of the Division Bench. Hence, he seeks dismissal of the writ petition."
  },
